{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https:\/\/json.schemastore.org\/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"Psalm","informationUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev","version":"5.26.1@d747f6500b38ac4f7dfc5edbcae6e4b637d7add0","rules":[{"id":"45","name":"MissingPropertyType","shortDescription":{"text":"MissingPropertyType"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/045","help":{"markdown":"# MissingPropertyType\n\nEmitted when a property is defined on a class without a type\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {\n    public $foo = 5;\n}\n```\n\nThis feature is available in PHP since version 7.4\n\nFor more information see:\n* [Properties](https:\/\/www.php.net\/manual\/en\/language.oop5.properties.php) in the PHP manual.\n* PHP RFC: [Typed Properties 2.0](https:\/\/wiki.php.net\/rfc\/typed_properties_v2)\n","text":"# MissingPropertyType\n\nEmitted when a property is defined on a class without a type\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {\n    public $foo = 5;\n}\n```\n\nThis feature is available in PHP since version 7.4\n\nFor more information see:\n* [Properties](https:\/\/www.php.net\/manual\/en\/language.oop5.properties.php) in the PHP manual.\n* PHP RFC: [Typed Properties 2.0](https:\/\/wiki.php.net\/rfc\/typed_properties_v2)\n"}},{"id":"154","name":"MissingParamType","shortDescription":{"text":"MissingParamType"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/154","help":{"markdown":"# MissingParamType\n\nEmitted when a function parameter has no type information associated with it\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo($a) : void {}\n```\n","text":"# MissingParamType\n\nEmitted when a function parameter has no type information associated with it\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo($a) : void {}\n```\n"}},{"id":"50","name":"MissingReturnType","shortDescription":{"text":"MissingReturnType"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/050","help":{"markdown":"# MissingReturnType\n\nEmitted when a function doesn't have a return type defined\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() {\n    return \"foo\";\n}\n```\n\nCorrect with:\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() : string {\n    return \"foo\";\n}\n```\n","text":"# MissingReturnType\n\nEmitted when a function doesn't have a return type defined\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() {\n    return \"foo\";\n}\n```\n\nCorrect with:\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() : string {\n    return \"foo\";\n}\n```\n"}},{"id":"87","name":"PossiblyUnusedMethod","shortDescription":{"text":"PossiblyUnusedMethod"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/087","help":{"markdown":"# PossiblyUnusedMethod\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm cannot find any calls to\na public or protected method.\n\nIf this method is used and part of the public API, annotate the containing class\nwith `@psalm-api`.\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {\n    public function foo() : void {}\n    public function bar() : void {}\n}\n(new A)->foo();\n```\n","text":"# PossiblyUnusedMethod\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm cannot find any calls to\na public or protected method.\n\nIf this method is used and part of the public API, annotate the containing class\nwith `@psalm-api`.\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {\n    public function foo() : void {}\n    public function bar() : void {}\n}\n(new A)->foo();\n```\n"}},{"id":"75","name":"UnusedClass","shortDescription":{"text":"UnusedClass"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/075","help":{"markdown":"# UnusedClass\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm cannot find any uses of a\ngiven class.\n\nIf this class is used and part of the public API, annotate it with `@psalm-api`.\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {}\nclass B {}\n$a = new A();\n```\n","text":"# UnusedClass\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm cannot find any uses of a\ngiven class.\n\nIf this class is used and part of the public API, annotate it with `@psalm-api`.\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {}\nclass B {}\n$a = new A();\n```\n"}},{"id":"84","name":"UnevaluatedCode","shortDescription":{"text":"UnevaluatedCode"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/084","help":{"markdown":"# UnevaluatedCode\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm encounters code that will not be evaluated\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() : void {\n    return;\n    $a = \"foo\";\n}\n```\n","text":"# UnevaluatedCode\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm encounters code that will not be evaluated\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() : void {\n    return;\n    $a = \"foo\";\n}\n```\n"}},{"id":"77","name":"UnusedVariable","shortDescription":{"text":"UnusedVariable"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/077","help":{"markdown":"# UnusedVariable\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm cannot find any references to a variable, once instantiated\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() : void {\n    $a = 5;\n    $b = 4;\n    echo $b;\n}\n```\n\nCan be suppressed by prefixing the variable name with an underscore:\n\n```php\n<?php\n\n$_a = 22;\n```\n","text":"# UnusedVariable\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm cannot find any references to a variable, once instantiated\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() : void {\n    $a = 5;\n    $b = 4;\n    echo $b;\n}\n```\n\nCan be suppressed by prefixing the variable name with an underscore:\n\n```php\n<?php\n\n$_a = 22;\n```\n"}},{"id":"122","name":"RedundantCondition","shortDescription":{"text":"RedundantCondition"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/122","help":{"markdown":"# RedundantCondition\n\nEmitted when conditional is redundant given previous assertions\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {}\nfunction foo(A $a) : ?A {\n    if ($a) return $a;\n    return null;\n}\n```\n","text":"# RedundantCondition\n\nEmitted when conditional is redundant given previous assertions\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {}\nfunction foo(A $a) : ?A {\n    if ($a) return $a;\n    return null;\n}\n```\n"}},{"id":"106","name":"UnresolvableInclude","shortDescription":{"text":"UnresolvableInclude"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/106","help":{"markdown":"# UnresolvableInclude\n\nEmitted when Psalm cannot figure out what specific file is being included\/required by PHP.\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction requireFile(string $s) : void {\n    require_once $s;\n}\n```\n","text":"# UnresolvableInclude\n\nEmitted when Psalm cannot figure out what specific file is being included\/required by PHP.\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction requireFile(string $s) : void {\n    require_once $s;\n}\n```\n"}},{"id":"12","name":"InvalidScalarArgument","shortDescription":{"text":"InvalidScalarArgument"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/012","help":{"markdown":"# InvalidScalarArgument\n\nEmitted when a scalar value is passed to a method that expected another scalar type.\n\nThis is only emitted in situations where Psalm can be sure that PHP tries to coerce one scalar type to another.\n\nIn all other cases `InvalidArgument` is emitted.\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo(int $i) : void {}\nfunction bar(string $s) : void {\n    if (is_numeric($s)) {\n        foo($s);\n    }\n}\n```\n","text":"# InvalidScalarArgument\n\nEmitted when a scalar value is passed to a method that expected another scalar type.\n\nThis is only emitted in situations where Psalm can be sure that PHP tries to coerce one scalar type to another.\n\nIn all other cases `InvalidArgument` is emitted.\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo(int $i) : void {}\nfunction bar(string $s) : void {\n    if (is_numeric($s)) {\n        foo($s);\n    }\n}\n```\n"}},{"id":"134","name":"PossiblyUnusedParam","shortDescription":{"text":"PossiblyUnusedParam"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/134","help":{"markdown":"# PossiblyUnusedParam\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm cannot find any uses of a particular parameter in a public\/protected method\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {\n    public function foo(int $a, int $b) : int {\n        return $a + 4;\n    }\n}\n\n$a = new A();\necho $a->foo(1, 2);\n```\n\nCan be suppressed by prefixing the parameter name with an underscore:\n\n```php\n<?php\nclass A {\n    public function foo(int $a, int $_b) : int {\n        return $a + 4;\n    }\n}\n```\n","text":"# PossiblyUnusedParam\n\nEmitted when `--find-dead-code` is turned on and Psalm cannot find any uses of a particular parameter in a public\/protected method\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nclass A {\n    public function foo(int $a, int $b) : int {\n        return $a + 4;\n    }\n}\n\n$a = new A();\necho $a->foo(1, 2);\n```\n\nCan be suppressed by prefixing the parameter name with an underscore:\n\n```php\n<?php\nclass A {\n    public function foo(int $a, int $_b) : int {\n        return $a + 4;\n    }\n}\n```\n"}},{"id":"2","name":"ForbiddenCode","shortDescription":{"text":"ForbiddenCode"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/002","help":{"markdown":"# ForbiddenCode\n\nEmitted when Psalm encounters a var_dump, exec or similar expression that may make your code more vulnerable\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nvar_dump(\"bah\");\n```\n\nThis functions list can be extended by configuring `forbiddenFunctions` in `psalm.xml`\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<psalm>\n    <!-- other configs -->\n\n    <forbiddenFunctions>\n        <function name=\"dd\"\/>\n        <function name=\"var_dump\"\/>\n    <\/forbiddenFunctions>\n<\/psalm>\n```\n","text":"# ForbiddenCode\n\nEmitted when Psalm encounters a var_dump, exec or similar expression that may make your code more vulnerable\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nvar_dump(\"bah\");\n```\n\nThis functions list can be extended by configuring `forbiddenFunctions` in `psalm.xml`\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<psalm>\n    <!-- other configs -->\n\n    <forbiddenFunctions>\n        <function name=\"dd\"\/>\n        <function name=\"var_dump\"\/>\n    <\/forbiddenFunctions>\n<\/psalm>\n```\n"}},{"id":"24","name":"UndefinedVariable","shortDescription":{"text":"UndefinedVariable"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/024","help":{"markdown":"# UndefinedVariable\n\nEmitted when referencing a variable that doesn't exist in a given function\u2019s scope\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() {\n    echo $a;\n}\n```\n","text":"# UndefinedVariable\n\nEmitted when referencing a variable that doesn't exist in a given function\u2019s scope\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo() {\n    echo $a;\n}\n```\n"}},{"id":"78","name":"PossiblyNullArgument","shortDescription":{"text":"PossiblyNullArgument"},"properties":{"tags":["maintainability"]},"helpUri":"https:\/\/psalm.dev\/078","help":{"markdown":"# PossiblyNullArgument\n\nEmitted when calling a function with a value that\u2019s possibly null when the function does not expect it\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo(string $s): void {}\nfoo(rand(0, 1) ? \"hello\" : null);\n```\n\n## Common Problem Cases\n\n### Using a Function Call inside `if`\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nif (is_string($cat->getName()) {\n    foo($cat->getName());\n}\n```\nThis fails since it's not guaranteed that subsequent calls to `$cat->getName()` always give the same result.\n\n#### Possible Solutions\n\nUse a variable:\n```php\n<?php\n\n$catName = $cat->getName();\nif (is_string($catName) {\n    foo($catName);\n}\nunset($catName);\n```\n\nOr add [`@psalm-mutation-free`](..\/..\/annotating_code\/supported_annotations.md#psalm-mutation-free) to the declaration of the function\n\n### Calling Another Function After `if`\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nif (is_string($cat->getName()) {\n    changeCat();\n    foo($cat->getName());\n}\n```\nThis fails since psalm cannot know if `changeCat()` does actually modify `$cat`.\n\n#### Possible Solutions\n\n* Add [`@psalm-mutation-free`](..\/..\/annotating_code\/supported_annotations.md#psalm-mutation-free) to the declaration of the other function (here: `changeCat()`) too\n* Use a variable: See above\n","text":"# PossiblyNullArgument\n\nEmitted when calling a function with a value that\u2019s possibly null when the function does not expect it\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nfunction foo(string $s): void {}\nfoo(rand(0, 1) ? \"hello\" : null);\n```\n\n## Common Problem Cases\n\n### Using a Function Call inside `if`\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nif (is_string($cat->getName()) {\n    foo($cat->getName());\n}\n```\nThis fails since it's not guaranteed that subsequent calls to `$cat->getName()` always give the same result.\n\n#### Possible Solutions\n\nUse a variable:\n```php\n<?php\n\n$catName = $cat->getName();\nif (is_string($catName) {\n    foo($catName);\n}\nunset($catName);\n```\n\nOr add [`@psalm-mutation-free`](..\/..\/annotating_code\/supported_annotations.md#psalm-mutation-free) to the declaration of the function\n\n### Calling Another Function After `if`\n\n```php\n<?php\n\nif (is_string($cat->getName()) {\n    changeCat();\n    foo($cat->getName());\n}\n```\nThis fails since psalm cannot know if `changeCat()` does actually modify `$cat`.\n\n#### Possible Solutions\n\n* Add [`@psalm-mutation-free`](..\/..\/annotating_code\/supported_annotations.md#psalm-mutation-free) to the declaration of the other function (here: `changeCat()`) too\n* Use a variable: See above\n"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"45","message":{"text":"Property App\\DatabaseVulnerability::$pdo does not have a declared type - consider mixed"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":11,"endLine":11,"startColumn":13,"endColumn":17}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $pdo has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":13,"endLine":13,"startColumn":33,"endColumn":37}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\DatabaseVulnerability::getUserById does not have a return type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":22,"endLine":22,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":32}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $id has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":22,"endLine":22,"startColumn":33,"endColumn":36}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\DatabaseVulnerability::searchUsers does not have a return type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":33,"endLine":33,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":32}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $name has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":33,"endLine":33,"startColumn":33,"endColumn":38}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\DatabaseVulnerability::deleteUser does not have a return type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":44,"endLine":44,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":31}}}]},{"ruleId":"87","message":{"text":"Cannot find any calls to method App\\DatabaseVulnerability::deleteUser"},"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":44,"endLine":44,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":31}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $userId has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DatabaseVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":44,"endLine":44,"startColumn":32,"endColumn":39}}}]},{"ruleId":"75","message":{"text":"Class App\\DeadCodeVulnerability is never used"},"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":9,"endLine":9,"startColumn":7,"endColumn":28}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\DeadCodeVulnerability::unreachableCode does not have a return type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":15,"endLine":15,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":36}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $value has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":15,"endLine":15,"startColumn":37,"endColumn":43}}}]},{"ruleId":"84","message":{"text":"Expressions after return\/throw\/continue"},"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":20,"endLine":20,"startColumn":9,"endColumn":40}}}]},{"ruleId":"84","message":{"text":"Expressions after return\/throw\/continue"},"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":21,"endLine":21,"startColumn":9,"endColumn":31}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\DeadCodeVulnerability::unusedMethod does not have a return type, expecting 'This method is never called'"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":28,"endLine":28,"startColumn":22,"endColumn":34}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\DeadCodeVulnerability::unusedVariable does not have a return type, expecting 'This is used'"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":37,"endLine":37,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":35}}}]},{"ruleId":"77","message":{"text":"$unused is never referenced or the value is not used"},"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":40,"endLine":40,"startColumn":9,"endColumn":16}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\DeadCodeVulnerability::alwaysTrueCondition does not have a return type, expecting 'Always true'|'Never reached'"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":49,"endLine":49,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":40}}}]},{"ruleId":"122","message":{"text":"Type 10 for $x is always >= 5"},"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":52,"endLine":52,"startColumn":13,"endColumn":19}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\DeadCodeVulnerability::infiniteLoop does not have a return type, expecting void"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/DeadCodeVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":63,"endLine":63,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":33}}}]},{"ruleId":"75","message":{"text":"Class App\\EntryPoint is never used"},"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/EntryPoint.php"},"region":{"startLine":12,"endLine":12,"startColumn":7,"endColumn":17}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\FileVulnerability::readFile does not have a return type, expecting false|string"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":15,"endLine":15,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":29}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $filename has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":15,"endLine":15,"startColumn":30,"endColumn":39}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\FileVulnerability::saveFile does not have a return type, expecting void"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":26,"endLine":26,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":29}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $path has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":26,"endLine":26,"startColumn":30,"endColumn":35}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $content has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":26,"endLine":26,"startColumn":37,"endColumn":45}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\FileVulnerability::loadTemplate does not have a return type, expecting void"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":36,"endLine":36,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":33}}}]},{"ruleId":"87","message":{"text":"Cannot find any calls to method App\\FileVulnerability::loadTemplate"},"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":36,"endLine":36,"startColumn":21,"endColumn":33}}}]},{"ruleId":"154","message":{"text":"Parameter $templateName has no provided type"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":36,"endLine":36,"startColumn":34,"endColumn":47}}}]},{"ruleId":"106","message":{"text":"Cannot resolve the given expression to a file path"},"level":"note","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src\/FileVulnerability.php"},"region":{"startLine":39,"endLine":39,"startColumn":9,"endColumn":39}}}]},{"ruleId":"50","message":{"text":"Method App\\FileVulnerability::ha